 ## Client, authentication, and offline boundaries
 
+### Phase 12 production source contract
+
+[ExecPlan 091](plans/091-production-runtime-and-deployment.md) governs the
+P12-01 source/local preflight. Production runtime requires explicit
+`BVA_MODE=production`, one canonical HTTPS application origin, loopback bind and
+port, an absolute built frontend directory, a dedicated loopback PostgreSQL
+database/runtime role with distinct owner/migration role, an ownership marker,
+and a protected proxy identity secret. Caddy terminates HTTPS and forwards to
+loopback FastAPI; it overwrites the identity header. Uvicorn keeps
+`proxy_headers=False`. FastAPI requires exact Host, exact approved browser or
+derived native Origin and the proxy identity before processing requests.
+Production auth emits Secure, HttpOnly, host-only, SameSite=Strict cookies and
+retains CSRF. Unknown `/api` routes remain JSON; private responses remain
+`no-store` and static bytes remain on the existing build allowlist.
+
+Production Android packages the shared React UI under the exact
+`https://android.<approved-host>` WebView origin and sends credentialed requests
+to `https://<approved-host>` under normal platform certificate validation.
+The two origins are same-site for Strict cookies. Backend credentialed CORS
+permits only that exact derived native origin. There is no production use of
+Capacitor `server.url`, TEST CA, localhost qualification transport, adb reverse,
+cleartext or native bearer replacement. These are source/local findings;
+production host, certificate and physical Android behavior remain later gates.
+
 Phase 7 introduces private authentication before any non-loopback access; current loopback Phase 1 contains no authentication. Choose and review the exact browser/wrapper session mechanism in Phase 7/9, keeping provider secrets server-side and protecting state changes.
 
